This repository is shared publicly so that authorized individuals can install
the Claude Code plugin it contains on their machines and use it as a working
tool in their daily work, including work performed in the course of their
employment or engagement.

Authorized individuals are:
  - employees and contractors of eVisions Advertising s.r.o., and
  - other persons authorized in writing by the copyright holder.

Authorized individuals may:
  - View the source code in this repository.
  - Clone the repository and install the plugin on machines they use for
    their work, including work on client projects and internal projects.
  - Use the plugin as part of their daily Claude Code setup on those
    machines.
  - Modify their local copy to fit their workflow.
  - Pull updates from this repository to refresh their installation.

Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, no one may:
  - Redistribute, republish, mirror, rehost, or otherwise share this
    repository or any part of it outside the authorized audience. The "fork"
    button on GitHub remains technically functional; that is a platform
    limitation, not a permission.
  - Use the plugin as the basis for a derivative work that is published,
    sold, sublicensed, or otherwise made available to third parties.
  - Package the plugin, or a recognisable derivative of it, into a product
    or service offering.
  - Use the source code or contents for training machine learning models.

The intent of this license: people who are authorized to use the plugin can
use it freely as a working tool. Taking it and turning it into something of
one's own, or passing it on outside the authorized audience, requires asking
first.

Optional companion plugins named in the documentation are not part of this
repository. They are installed from their authors' own sources and are
governed by their authors' licenses.

